== Controls that distinguish the interfaces
- Generic division by c in (N,c*x) fails at c(p)=p,N=p,x=1. Clearing c restores divisibility, with height charged.
- I=(x+c*y), clipped to span(x), is globally free/monic but its clipped kernel changes on a bad fiber. Global saturation is not clipped base change.
- Rows p and p(p+1) have equal p-local span but different integer determinant. A prime-to-p index is not free.
- Repeated equations, equal-support corruption and x-only signed lifts do not establish joint gain, a root, or a group relation. Valid equations alone need not give zero-dimensional extraction.

All controls were checked manually/source-wise, not executed against software. Integer lifts, basis index and bit sizes must be charged as they actually occur; large trailing coefficients need not universally change a triangular determinant.

